# THE FREEZE-ARM LEDGER — every decision `type_is_freeze` makes, and the axis
# that pins it.
#
# `type_is_freeze` (src/compiler/mlir_gen_types.cpp) is the entire soundness
# argument for `noalias`+`readonly` on a shared `&T`. Its IR gate pinned FIVE
# axes against a predicate that makes SEVENTEEN verdicts, and that gap was
# MEASURED, not supposed: replacing the element recursion in the TUPLE arm with
# `return true` moved `&(Cell<i64>, i64)` from `ptr noundef align 8` to
# `ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8` — a real noalias+readonly on a pointee
# holding a Cell — with all five axes green and L2 at 1881/1881.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT THE POPULATION. `freeze_arm_coverage.py` DERIVES the
# population from the artifacts — the Kind enumerators from
# include/logos/compiler/sema.hpp, the verdict sites from the predicate's own
# body — and holds it against these rows in both directions. A new Kind, a new
# arm, an axis renamed out from under a row: each is red by arithmetic. Writing
# a longer list here fixes nothing; the list is the thing being checked.
#
# ── SECTION `KINDS_TOTAL` ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How many enumerators `enum class Kind` declares. Named + defaulted must equal
# it exactly, so a Kind cannot arrive without somebody deciding which arm it
# belongs to.
KINDS_TOTAL
50
#
# ── SECTION `DEFAULTED` ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Kinds with no `case` label, which reach `default: return false`. That
# answer is CONSERVATIVE — a non-Freeze verdict costs an optimization and never
# soundness — so this is the safe place for a Kind to land. It is still a
# decision, and moving one out of here changes the compiler's answer for every
# value of that kind.
#
# `TypeVar` is the live one: it is what the HRTB residue axis exercises.
DEFAULTED
AssocType
CfgSlotType
ConstVar
Error
FnItem
Generic
ImplTrait
InferredType
TypeVar
WStaticLit
#
# ── SECTION `NAMED` ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `<Kind>\t<arm ordinal>` — which verdict site each explicitly-cased Kind
# reaches first. The ordinal is the site's position in the ARMS section below.
#
# NOTE ON `Struct`/`ZonedStruct` = 8 and `Enum` = 14: the ordinal is the FIRST
# verdict inside the block the case label opens (the UnsafeCell lang-item test
# and the payload-loop rejection respectively), not the block's final answer.
# That is the mechanical rule — first verdict at or after the label — and it is
# what makes the mapping derivable instead of judged.
NAMED
Array	5
Bool	3
Char	3
Closure	4
DstRef	4
Enum	14
F32	3
F64	3
FloatLit	3
FnPtr	4
I128	3
I16	3
I24	3
I32	3
I56	3
I64	3
I8	3
IntLit	3
Isize	3
MutRef	4
Never	3
Ptr	4
Ref	4
Slice	4
Struct	8
TaggedPtr	4
TraitObject	4
Tuple	6
U128	3
U16	3
U24	3
U32	3
U56	3
U64	3
U8	3
UnsizedDyn	4
UnsizedSlice	4
Usize	3
Void	3
ZonedStruct	8
#
# ── SECTION `ARMS` ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `<ordinal>\t<arm id>\t<axis[,axis…] | NO-AXIS:<reason>>\t<verdict text>`
#
# The verdict text is whitespace-normalised source, NOT a line number — a
# reformat must not go red, an added decision must. Ordinals are positions in
# the predicate's body, so inserting an arm shifts the ones after it and the
# diff names the insertion.
#
# An axis id must have an `; AXIS <id>` marker with at least one CHECK line in
# tests/logos/ir/param_attrs_freeze_lattice.check. `NO-AXIS:` needs a reason,
# and the gate PRINTS every one of them on a green run, so the coverage number
# cannot be read as total.
ARMS
1	null-typeref	NO-AXIS:a null TypeRef is internal compiler state; no source program produces one, and the answer (false) is the conservative direction	return false;
2	anyval-shortcircuit	axis_anyval	return true;
3	scalar-kinds	axis_scalar	return true;
4	indirection-stop	axis_ptr_field	return true;
5	array-elements	axis_array	return !tv.elem() ? true : type_is_freeze(tv.elem(), seen);
6	tuple-element-nonfreeze	axis_tuple_cell,axis_tuple_nested	return false;
7	tuple-all-freeze	axis_tuple_plain	return true;
8	unsafecell-lang-item	axis_unsafecell_item	return false;
9	struct-cycle-guard	NO-AXIS:unreachable from source — a Logos struct cannot contain itself by value, so every self-reference passes through an indirection and arm 4 returns before `seen` is consulted; axis_selfref_cell/plain pin the ANSWER for a recursive shape but not this branch	return true;
10	struct-init	axis_selfref_plain	bool frozen = true;
11	struct-unresolved	NO-AXIS:UNPROBED, not proven unreachable — no source shape has been found that reaches `find_struct_def_it == end()` for a Kind::Struct; the answer (false) is conservative, so a miss here costs an optimization, never soundness	frozen = false;
12	struct-field-nonfreeze	axis_nested2,axis_selfref_cell,axis_tuple_field	frozen = false;
13	struct-verdict	axis_tuple_field_plain	return frozen;
14	enum-payload-nonfreeze	axis_opt_cell	return false;
15	enum-payload-freeze	axis_opt_plain	return true;
16	enum-clike-fallback	axis_clike	return true;
17	default-unknown-kind	axis_residue	return false;
#
# ── SECTION `EXTRA_AXES` ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Axes that pin a PROPERTY of the predicate rather than one verdict site. They
# are listed so the reverse direction still closes: every `; AXIS` marker in the
# .check is claimed by exactly one row, here or above, and an axis orphaned by a
# rename is red.
EXTRA_AXES
axis_generic	the answer is keyed on the INSTANCE, not the definition: one generic, two monomorphisations, opposite answers. Not a single site — every arm below it is reached per-instance.
